  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "Mallory's snow goggles were in his pocket, not his eyes. Everest, and he had been missing for seventy-five years.",
        "visual_query": "mount everest north face",
        "visual_fallback": "everest summit"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Mallory and Sandy Irvine went up on the eighth of June, 1924. Noel Odell watched two dots move on the ridge, then cloud closed.",
        "visual_query": "1920s himalayan mountaineering expedition",
        "visual_fallback": "old expedition"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Conrad Anker found him in 1999 just under twenty-seven thousand feet, a rope still knotted at his waist. Goggles come off when the light goes. So was he coming down from the top?",
        "visual_query": "everest high altitude snow ridge",
        "visual_fallback": "snowy ridge"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Probably not. The camera that would prove it was not on him, and neither was the photograph of his wife he meant to leave up there.",
        "visual_query": "1920s expedition camera gear",
        "visual_fallback": "vintage camera"
      },
      {
        "narration": "In 2024 a glacier far below gave up a boot with Irvine's name tape inside. The camera is still up there.",
        "visual_query": "rongbuk glacier himalaya ice",
        "visual_fallback": "glacier ice"
      }
    ],
